    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d101">

                <pb facs="0197" n="165" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v11/pg165"/>

                <head>101. Telegram From the Mission at the United
                        Nations to the Department of State<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d101-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic">New
                                York</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1958-06-20T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 20, 1958—6
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>1540. Re: Lebanon. In discussing situation in Lebanon with Mission officer today,
                    Chechetkin (UN) said Soviets had strong fear
                    that, under UK pressure, US would land Marines in
                    Lebanon. He stated that, if this occurred, Soviets would immediately send
                    “volunteers” to oppose such action.</p>
                <p>Chechetkin, now Chief UN Commercial Management
                    Services, was formerly Counselor Soviet UNDel and worked closely with
                        Zarubin during GA
                    sessions. We believe Soviet Delegation continues use him as channel for
                    conveying Soviet views to US.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold"
                            >Barco</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d101-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d101-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 783A.00/6–2058. Confidential.
                    Repeated to Moscow, Cairo, and Beirut.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
